dropped the body
found no match for symbol
--
N5008 [comparisons.three.way]: `std::compare_three_way()(p, q)' on two
pointers to the same class is the built-in `p <=> q' (strong_ordering);
libc++ 18 constrains the call operator with `three_way_comparable_with<_Tp,
_Up>' and defines it in <__compare/compare_three_way.h>.  With libc++ the
call fails ("found no match for symbol 'operator()'" at line 28) and the
translation unit is rejected; this is libc++'s error_category::operator<=>
(`compare_three_way()(this, std::addressof(__rhs))'), dropped in every
libc++ C++20 test (audit residue item 2, round 162).  With libstdc++ the
same program passes (--object-bits 12 is for the locale machinery pulled
in by <memory>).
